# Product engineering

Continue the shipped implementation. Do not replace domains, routes, or schema history with a new design.

Prioritize, in this order:

1. Behavior a customer can complete: CRM, Inbox, knowledge, approvals, workflows, campaigns, and billing.
2. Interface quality against `design-reference/ATLAS Workspace Overview.zip` and `docs/UI1_INTERFACE_RECONCILIATION.md`.
3. Real provider activation in `docs/provider-activation.md`. A sandbox double is not a live connection.

Use the vocabulary already in the code: `organization`, `membership`, `session`, `inquiry`, `approval`, `provider`, and `integration`. Describe capabilities and acceptance criteria. Do not name product work as a "Day N" milestone. Do not rename persisted slugs, migration identifiers, or fixture subjects to chase wording.

